//RS // D-UNITLIT1: unit-suffix numeric literals (`500ms`) are not an enumerable
//RS // keyword — the lexer resolves a literal's identifier suffix against
//RS // #UnitFamily members in scope (MARKER_UNIT_FAMILY, D-QUAL3). One fixed rule:
//RS /// D-UNITLIT1: a literal suffix shaped `e` + digits is reserved for float
//RS /// exponent notation (`1e5`) and may never resolve as a unit name.
//RS pub const UNIT_SUFFIX_EXPONENT_RESERVED: &str = "e"; // D-UNITLIT1
//RS /// D-TYPE2-IMAG1=A (ratified 2026-08-06): numeric suffix `i` mints the
//RS /// imaginary component of Complex through the existing unit-literal path;
//RS /// bare `i` remains an ordinary identifier.
//RS pub const UNIT_SUFFIX_IMAGINARY: &str = "i";
//RS 
//RS // D-TRAILBLOCK2=A (amends D-TRAILBLOCK1): no new token — code arguments are
//RS // ordinary `() -> { … }` lambdas inside call parentheses. A bare `{` after a
//RS // call is E0335 (retired trailing-block sugar), not a new lexical form.
//RS // D-DESTRUCT1: no new token — reuses the D-DOTCTOR1 `.{` sigil in pattern
//RS // position and `..` (OP_RANGE) as the now-mandatory partial-pattern rest
//RS // marker.
//RS // D-CHAINCMP1: no new token — same-direction `<`/`<=`/`>`/`>=` chains are a
//RS // parser/sema desugaring (`0 <= sev < 10` → `0 <= sev && sev < 10`, middle
//RS // operand evaluated once).
//RS // D-CLIFLAG1: the struct-level CLI-derive marker and field-level doc marker
//RS // spellings ride D-CONTRACTCASE1/D-VERDICT-732-1 (formerly D-MARKERMOVE1) —
//RS // constants land with them.
//RS // D-EFFBUDGET1: `effects`/`allow`/`deny`/`grants` are package.jet manifest
//RS // keys (jet_pkg_model::Package), not language tokens; effect names reuse D-EFF4.
//RS // D-ANY-JAI1 + D-VARARGBOUND1: reuses D-VARIADIC1 `...T`; multi-trait
//RS // bounds use the owner-amended list form (`T: [A, B]`, `...items: [A, B]`).
//RS // D-TRAIT-OVERLOAD1=A: no new token — `trait Name: [A, B] { … }` reuses the
//RS // D-VARARGBOUND1 bound list after a trait name to list the traits it builds
//RS // on (a single one stays bare: `trait Name: A`). A bound on such a trait
//RS // admits the listed traits' operators and methods in generic bodies.
//RS // D-UFCS1 (B), D-POINTERCHAIN1 (A), D-ERRCTX1 (D): no typeable surface.
//RS 
